    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d81-a3">

                <pb facs="0204" n="194" sameAs="frus:frus1864p1/pg194"/>

                <head>Mr. Moran to Mr.
                        Seward.</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Legation of the United
                                States,</hi><hi rendition="#italic"> London,</hi></placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1864-02-20"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >February</hi> 20, 1864.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir:</hi> By direction of Mr. Adams, I have the honor
                    to forward herewith, out of the regular course, a copy of The Index, of the 18th
                    instant, a paper in the <pb facs="0205" n="195" xml:id="pg195"/> interest of the
                    rebels, published in London. At page 107 will be found a narrative of the recent
                    attempt on the part of a number of the insurgents to invade the United States
                    from Canada. To this Mr. Adams requests me to call your special attention.</p>
                <p>I have the honor to be, sir, with great respect, your obedient servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>BENJ. MORAN, <hi rendition="#italic">Assistant Secretary of
                            Legation.</hi></signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>Hon. <hi rendition="#small-caps">William H. Seward,</hi>
                        <hi rendition="#italic">Secretary of State, Washington, D. C.</hi></p>
                </postscript>


                <xi:include href="d81-a3-a1.xml" xpointer="d81-a3-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
